> *"Education functions as an asymmetric financial asset strictly when its acquisition cost does not exceed the risk-adjusted Net Present Value (NPV) of future wage distributions. When funded via high-coupon unsecured leverage against unranked vocational credentials, it ceases to be human capital accumulation and mutates into a predatory subprime liability."*
> 
> — **Finesse Institutional Research Cell | Academic Whitepaper Series (Ref: FOE-AUDIT-2026/09)**

